    {
      "id": "claim_bcc478242c8643dabbfe30e448e6b1e6",
      "statement": "OpenWiki 0.5.x treats mermaid and jsdom as optional peer dependencies; when they are absent the generator falls back to a weaker built-in fence check, silently rewrites any Mermaid diagram it cannot verify into a plain text fence, exits 0, and passes every gate — leaving a quietly degraded diagram as the only symptom.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/dev-environment-setup.md#L109-L114",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:969dbf6dd1156bdf46d968f4b62e88d58c76eaa87d71e86c7f81d36c9848a764:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_56e5d718ae014a25b614be6ca38921b6",
      "statement": "The host toolchain for MovieCollectionManager requires Node.js (LTS, floor >=22.13 set by root package.json engines.node), pnpm via Corepack (the exact version pinned by root package.json packageManager, currently pnpm@12.13.0), Nx (workspace, via pnpm nx), Rust stable, Python 3.13 with uv, Docker Desktop 24+, OpenJDK 17, and Android SDK Platform 36 (the compileSdk the pinned React Native's Gradle version catalog sets) with Build Tools and an Emulator API 34 system image; these are all pre-provisioned in the devcontainer toolchain image, which bakes Node from a node:24-bookworm base, resolves pnpm from packageManager via Corepack, and installs the android-34 SDK platform/emulator packages for its ANDROID_API=34 build arg. Exact Node/pnpm patch pins otherwise drift independently across CI and Docker contexts in this repo and are reconciled by scripts/check-toolchain-consistency.mjs rather than being fixed values.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://.devcontainer/toolchain.Dockerfile#L182-L212",
