    {
      "id": "claim_a7014ab5ed5e4589b7e8e47526107299",
      "statement": "The repository's Node requirement is the root package.json engines.node floor (>=22.13), and scripts/check-toolchain-consistency.mjs enforces it: it scans every workflow node-version: and every FROM node:<v> in the pinned files (.forgejo/workflows, .devcontainer/toolchain.Dockerfile, frontend/mcm-app/Dockerfile) and fails any pin below the floor, reporting an unparseable pin such as lts/* rather than passing it silently. The floor came from pnpm 11's own engines (>=22.13); pnpm 12 declares only >=18, and the floor was deliberately not lowered, so it must be raised whenever packageManager moves to a manager with a higher floor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://package.json#L6-L9",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0c887da054a266b9a0bfcf8fc0516635e023ef68318fc8140ba2a80d9f5d6c19:"
