    {
      "id": "claim_c2cb8d139e1f4f0bb979bb4c637b5d1b",
      "statement": "The OpenWiki generator's version is pinned in two places that must agree: the dev container's toolchain image installs it globally (`npm install -g openwiki@<v> mermaid jsdom`, since there is no repository checkout at image-build time), while the CI wiki-maintain job has no generator baked in and installs the same three exact pins from the committed lockfile in tools/openwiki-generator/ with `pnpm --dir tools/openwiki-generator install --frozen-lockfile`. tools/openwiki-generator is its own pnpm workspace root, outside the root workspace globs, with a three-day minimumReleaseAge cooldown enforced at both resolve and install time so a lockfile regeneration cannot pull in a freshly published transitive. scripts/__tests__/wiki-maintain.guard.test.mjs reads the container's real install command line against the locked manifest and fails if the versions or the mermaid/jsdom peer set differ, and renovate.json moves both halves in one grouped PR.",
      "evidence": [
